      "worked": "Bob keeps the original right half, reflects a copy across the $y$-axis, then reflects every part below the $x$-axis upwards.\n\nMary reflects the negative outputs upwards first, then keeps the resulting right half and reflects a copy across the $y$-axis.\n\nBoth give $y=|f(|x|)|$ on the same domain. Changing an output's sign does not change which half is copied, so the correct final graphs always agree.",
